  "body": "### Summary\n\nLOT-109 (#200, image viewer and HD gallery) may start before capture #134 lands (operator decision, 2026-10-29). Until then the lot follows legacy and the LOT-056 host table, and lists #134 as *pending capture*. When #134 lands, this review checks the merged lot against the capture and fixes any difference.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **What #134 settles for LOT-109:** how `reho.st` serves an image fetched without cookies, with and without a `Referer` (LOT-056 spec, \"Pending capture\" 1). The viewer's full-resolution fetch must follow what the capture shows.\n- Add a test of the lot on the new fixture.\n- If the capture contradicts what the lot assumed, fix the lot.\n- Update the LOT-109 and LOT-056 specs (\"Pending capture\") and HFR-PROTOCOL §6c.\n- If the capture confirms the assumption, close this issue with a comment naming the fixture and the test.\n\n### Protocol for whoever claims LOT-109\n\nComment here once, from the lot's session:\n- **If you are a CLI session with capture access** (the maintainer's Mac, LOT-001 kit): do #134 first, then name the capture PR and the fixture ids.\n- **Otherwise:** state:\n  - what the lot assumes, with the legacy file:line;\n  - where the spec lists the pending capture;\n  - the lot's PR.\n\n### Depends on\n\n- #134 (capture)\n- LOT-109 (#200) merged\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A test of LOT-109 runs on the #134 fixture and passes. It is shown to fail if the lot's assumption is reversed.\n- [ ] The \"Pending capture\" item is removed from the LOT-109 and LOT-056 specs (or rewritten with what remains), and HFR-PROTOCOL §6c records the verified fact.\n- [ ] If the user-visible behaviour changes, `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` has a row for it.\n- [ ] The PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #200`.\n\n### Model\n\nAny reviewer whose model differs from LOT-109's author model (AGENTS.md §6).",
